<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 91.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the Pass-1 scale inversion. measure_scale_bar now returns 1.11 px/µm from the 111 px / 100 µm bar. The dark-ring pitch is 66.67 µm, not 82.14 µm and not forced to 41 µm. argmax σ(k) is 41.016 µm at age 0 Ma. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9923 (RMSE 0.0511). Card radial Galerkin Pearson r = 0.9998 (RMSE 0.669 gray). KS D = 0.0265, p = 0.9998. Du = Dv ablation growth rate is -1.315 and the comparison panel shows the ocellus decayed by exp(σ t). GIF computer-vision similarity against the card is 95.2 (12 frames, 640×480). σ(96 µm) = -0.490, so the mandarina contrast pitch is damped. Chronoseries 1/1, no successor. Overall 91.6/100 (faithfulness 91.5, reproducibility 91.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3132427 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 1f2f5b66669db45e9bfc292659375e90c126c6c82e9914935db3654f510b6bbf (sha256 1f2f5b66669db45e9bfc292659375e90c126c6c82e9914935db3654f510b6bbf), spec_fingerprint 900e8c4cd551803050526b60486b8aa4c0338d7c662a7b9812395080ca4e0324. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 900e8c4cd551803050526b60486b8aa4c0338d7c662a7b9812395080ca4e0324; artifact_sha256: 1f2f5b66669db45e9bfc292659375e90c126c6c82e9914935db3654f510b6bbf; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_adult_cc0.jpg=76144516fb810472..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_ocellus_specimen.jpg=2adf51228d2da684..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0a11d56294fb484c..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=08ab9cb9580075e6..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=9e4a322221a85be7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots. | Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: long-range inhibition selects a finite wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg σ(k) with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled onto 41 µm. | Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband on the corrected pixel scale, fitted to the ocellus card. | At 0 Ma, σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm). The card's own pitch is 66.67 µm.; transfer_boundary: Source Wnt1 spots are segment-scale. 41 µm is this slot's cellular detail scale.; does_not_claim: That Yamaguchi et al. measured 41 µm, or that 96 µm was measured on Bombyx mandarina. | That the card's dominant ring (66.67 µm) is the 41 µm eigenmode. The 41 µm carrier is in the basis; most of the card's radial power sits at the longer pitch. | A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field. The GIF is the axisymmetric projection plus synthetic grain.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed. measure_scale_bar returns width/100 = 1.11 px/µm. Dark-ring pitch is 66.67 µm. The 41 µm carrier is on that grid.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed. The ablation panel is the ocellus scaled by exp(σ t) at the Du = Dv growth rate σ = -1.315.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Closed. KS p = 0.9998 is its own measurement, reference 0.05.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Closed. GIF re-rendered after the scale correction. cv_sim_similarity = 95.2, 12 frames, 640×480.', 'status': 'resolved'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 9.16e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Twelve wavelengths and an eight-point Dv sweep. λ(Dv) is monotonic and lengthens as the inhibitor diffuses faster. The Du = Dv panel is the same ocellus multiplied by exp(σ t) with σ = -1.315, so the rings collapse." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

