<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Bombyx mori)",
        "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Bombyx mori morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bombyx mori specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bombyx mori" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field. The GIF is the axisymmetric projection plus synthetic grain.",
        "does_not_claim: That Yamaguchi et al. measured 41 µm, or that 96 µm was measured on Bombyx mandarina.",
        "does_not_claim: That the card's dominant ring (66.67 µm) is the 41 µm eigenmode. The 41 µm carrier is in the basis; most of the card's radial power sits at the longer pitch.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: At 0 Ma, σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm). The card's own pitch is 66.67 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband on the corrected pixel scale, fitted to the ocellus card.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg σ(k) with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled onto 41 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: long-range inhibition selects a finite wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots.",
        "transfer_boundary: Source Wnt1 spots are segment-scale. 41 µm is this slot's cellular detail scale." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Bombyx mori" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Bombyx" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; output: docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Bombyx mori; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots. | Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: long-range inhibition selects a finite wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg σ(k) with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled onto 41 µm. | Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband on the corrected pixel scale, fitted to the ocellus card. | At 0 Ma, σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm). The card's own pitch is 66.67 µm.; transfer_boundary: Source Wnt1 spots are segment-scale. 41 µm is this slot's cellular detail scale.; does_not_claim: That Yamaguchi et al. measured 41 µm, or that 96 µm was measured on Bombyx mandarina. | That the card's dominant ring (66.67 µm) is the 41 µm eigenmode. The 41 µm carrier is in the basis; most of the card's radial power sits at the longer pitch. | A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field. The GIF is the axisymmetric projection plus synthetic grain.]; phenomenon_size: 32 µm (3.2e-05 m, log10=-4.495 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 32 µm to 9.2 cm): 32 µm:bombyx-mori-bioelectric-polarity, 114 µm:bombyx-mori-vertex-packing, 2.0 mm:bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength, 3.9 mm:bombyx-mori-clock-wavefront, 6.7 mm:bombyx-mori-morphogen-condensation, 8.6 mm:bombyx-mori-flux-canalization, 9.4 mm:bombyx-mori-elastic-buckling, 1.1 cm:bombyx-mori-branching-tree" ;
